{
  "note": [
    "The Repair Room's fabric, cut from the one Lawanda layout in scripts/fabric-lawanda.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. REPAIR-ROOM v3 with the 2026-09-17 geometry pass: 10 x 3.8 x 10, the eye at the middle, its floor 4.0 m below Systems Corridor West's. Dimly lit: three warm lamps at 5, against the Infirmary's 14.",
    "SOUTH IS A HIGH SLOT, NOT A DOORWAY -- 1.5 x 2.3 centred 2.65, spanning 1.5 to 3.8 m, its sill 0.1 m BELOW the eye and its head the ceiling, with no lintel. The corridor's floor and everything standing on it are out of sight. What fills the opening is the stair: the last 2.1 m of the flight stands inside this room, its foot on this floor 2.9 m from the eye, its treads crossing the wall plane 1.575 m up, climbing south into the shaft between the concrete sides 1.5 m apart, the stepped soffit rising from this ceiling to the corridor's 2.0 m head. The warm lamp in the shaft is 6.08 m out and 4.4 m up and needs a slope of 0.46 where the head allows 0.44: THE FITTING IS JUST ABOVE THE LINTEL AND NOT IN SIGHT, and what shows is the light it throws down the shaft's walls -- the one light in this dim room that is not its own.",
    "At the top, through the well's 1.5 x 2.0 head, a band only 4.1 degrees high does reach Systems Corridor West (slopes 0.357 to 0.44 against the aperture's -0.02 to 0.44): the guard rails round the well, then the corridor's CEILING, then the top of its far south wall about 3.3 m up, in a strip 3.5 m wide 16 m from the eye. Its Infirmary mouth, its east mouth, its southwest mouth to the Fork and its floor are all below that band, which is why the Infirmary, the hallway east and the walk to the Fork are not in this scene at all.",
    "North, the robot hole: 0.8 x 0.85 with its sill 0.125 m up, and behind it a concrete duct 2.0 m deep closed at its end. It is EMPTY IN EVERY STATE -- the good board starts inside it with NDESCBIT and INVISIBLE and is never drawn there, so no board, no glint and no contents belong in it before or after Floyd's retrieval. The room itself: the storage cabinets west, the machines east, Achilles face down off the stair's foot."
  ],
